= The Comparative Framework & Shared Historical Foundations

In an increasingly globalized world, nations actively analyze and compare their development trajectories with their geographic neighbors. Regional economic groupings—such as the *South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC)*, *Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN)*, *BRICS*, *G20*, and the *European Union (EU)*—reflect the growing economic interdependence among neighboring nations.

== 1. Why Compare India, China, and Pakistan?
India, China, and Pakistan provide the ideal comparative development model in economics because all three nations started their modern developmental journeys from remarkably similar socio-economic baselines in the late 1940s:

